(vector (map (:adr/authoritative_for (vector "dossier.houjin-bangou real live client" "cloud-itonami canonical business-entity registry (DUNS-Number analog)")), (:adr/topic "isic-8291-houjin-bangou-canonical-business-registry"), (:adr/related (vector "adr-2607110400" "adr-2607150100" "adr-2607172600")), (:adr/status "accepted"), (:adr/id "adr-2607182200-isic-8291-houjin-bangou-canonical-business-registry"), (:adr/doc_type "adr"), (:adr/last_verified "2026-07-18"), (:adr/body "# ADR-2607182200: cloud-itonami-isic-8291 dossier -- real houjin-bangou (\u6cd5\u4eba\u756a\u53f7) live client, cloud-itonami's canonical business-entity registry\n\n**Status**: accepted\n**Date**: 2026-07-18\n**Deciders**: Jun Kawasaki (owner directive: \\\"cloud-itonami \u3068\u3057\u3066\u3061\u3083\u3093\u3068\u8a2d\u8a08\u3057\u3066, duns number \u306e\u3088\u3046\u306b\\\", following the outreach-list-sourcing conversation where the owner correctly redirected away from ad-hoc web-collected prospect lists toward a canonical, DUNS-Number-like business-identity system)\n**Scope**: `orgs/cloud-itonami/cloud-itonami-isic-8291` (child commit `ce3d8d578f45`), west pin advance (`cb599f12a70e`->`ce3d8d578f45`).\n\n## Context\n\nThe owner asked, in effect: \\\"cloud-itonami already has a DUNS-Number-like canonical business-entity registry design somewhere, doesn't it?\\\" Investigation confirmed: yes -- `cloud-itonami-isic-8291` (\\\"dossier\\\", ADR-2607110400) is exactly this: a governed corporate/compliance-intelligence actor holding canonical company/official entities, with an R0 source-basis catalog (`dossier.facts`) naming real, public, official registries as the ONLY acceptable citation basis for a fact. It already had REAL live clients for UK Companies House (`dossier.companies-house`, ADR addendum 5), GLEIF LEI (`dossier.gleif`) and SEC EDGAR (`dossier.sec-edgar`) -- but `:jpn-houjin-bangou` (Japan's National Tax Agency Corporate Number, the single most relevant registry for this portfolio's Japan-jurisdiction SMB flagships) was cataloged since the original ADR yet never wired to a real client (`:access :public-api`, no `:live-capable?` flag at all).\n\nThis ADR closes that specific gap -- giving cloud-itonami a REAL, government-grounded canonical business identifier for Japan, the same architectural role DUNS Number plays for Dun & Bradstreet: every dossier company entity gets a stable `jpn-<corporateNumber>` id, resolvable against the real government registry, that any other cloud-itonami actor (5820 CRM's Account, 7810's prospect intake, etc.) can reference instead of inventing its own ad-hoc company identity.\n\n## Decision\n\nBuilt `dossier.houjin-bangou` (mirrors `dossier.companies-house`'s exact structure and honesty discipline):\n\n- Real request/response shapes sourced from the actual public API spec (base URL `https://api.houjin-bangou.nta.go.jp`, `/4/num` + `/4/name` endpoints, full `corporation` response schema) -- cross-checked against the open-source TypeScript wrapper `totechite/houjinbangou-api-wrapper`'s `src/types.ts`, not guessed.\n- Server is XML-only (`type=12`); parsed with `clojure.xml` (JVM core, zero new dependency).\n- Wired into `dossier.live-store` as a new `LiveJpnStore` decorator + `jpn-store` constructor, chained into the 0/1-arg convenience constructors via a new 5-arg explicit-control arity. All existing 2/3/4-arg call shapes are unchanged byte-for-byte (regression-tested).\n- `dossier.facts`'s `:jpn-houjin-bangou` catalog entry gains `:live-capable? true` (a static fact about code existing, same convention the GBR entry already documents).\n\n## Honest gap: NOT live-verified\n\nUnlike Companies House (instant self-serve API key) and GLEIF (keyless), houjin-bangou requires a National Tax Agency **Application ID via a ~2-4 week manual registration** (the applicant's real name/organization, email-based application to `invoice-web-api@nta.go.jp`) -- **this cannot be self-served or applied for by an agent on the operator's behalf**, it registers the operator's own identity with a government agency. This client is offline-tested against realistic fixture XML matching the real documented schema (113/492 assertions green across the whole actor, up from 96/424; clj-kondo clean) but has never made a real network call, because no Application ID was available in this session.\n\n**Owner follow-up needed**: apply for the free Application ID at https://www.houjin-bangou.nta.go.jp/webapi/ (2-4 week turnaround), then set `HOUJIN_BANGOU_APPLICATION_ID`. Once set, `dossier.live-store/live-store`'s 0/1-arg constructors pick it up automatically -- no further code change needed.\n\n## Consequences / next steps (not done in this ADR)\n\n- This closes the \\\"canonical business-entity registry\\\" infrastructure gap. It does NOT yet solve 7810's original prospect-acquisition need end-to-end -- houjin-bangou looks up a company you already have a name for (or a known corporate number); it does not browse/discover companies by industry (the API has no ISIC/SIC-equivalent filter). Finding real candidate small employment agencies to look up still needs a separate, legitimate source -- Japan's MHLW publishes a public list of licensed \u6709\u6599\u8077\u696d\u7d39\u4ecb\u4e8b\u696d\u8005 (licensed private employment agencies), which was flagged as the most on-target candidate but not yet investigated/fetched in this session.\n- Wiring 5820's `Account`/`Lead` entities to reference a canonical `jpn-<corporateNumber>` dossier id (instead of an ad-hoc local id) is a natural next step, not done here.\n- kagi/1Password home for `HOUJIN_BANGOU_APPLICATION_ID` once obtained: not yet created (nothing to store until the owner completes registration).\n"), (:adr/deciders (vector "Jun Kawasaki")), (:adr/date "2026-07-18"), (:db/id -1), (:adr/authoritative true), (:adr/title "ADR-2607182200: cloud-itonami-isic-8291 dossier -- real houjin-bangou live client, canonical business-entity registry (DUNS Number analog)"), (:adr/source-format "edn")))